                <l xml:id="m-793656f6-aef7-48b4-ad28-8fbd8cef1c69" facs="#m-d4ee2e60-26f0-43a5-bf74-8e5cd23f74b6" label="text-like">The Paschal Vigil</l><l xml:id="m-39af0c87-d357-4c0e-b441-40c8aeb1906c" facs="#m-b1110ee2-8ec4-4679-a3c2-fa3d58114777" label="ambiguous">TTGRE</l><l xml:id="m-de0d31fa-9127-404b-8aa4-ba8aefb72c09" facs="#m-aeb962e1-9371-47eb-bffd-fdfce805a461" label="lyrics-like">Accipe lámpadem ardéntem, et irreprehensibilis custódi Baptis¬</l><l xml:id="m-3869cea7-4aa1-4426-95d1-8086ee4591d6" facs="#m-8c282588-bc0f-461f-a482-74f8c555d8f3" label="lyrics-like">mum tuum: serva Dei mandáta, ut, cum Dóminus vénerit ad</l><l xml:id="m-c13644c8-edda-49ed-bb09-a9fa0f9b0d1c" facs="#m-5e694deb-f364-4205-bdab-b0bb9500b973" label="lyrics-like">núptias, possis occúrrere ei una cum ómnibus sanctis in aula</l><l xml:id="m-8fc0d953-5828-416d-b7f8-505ba3d18241" facs="#m-1274ea6c-f32e-4a7c-88fc-fd25d3f25a13" label="lyrics-like">caclésti et vivas in saécula saeculórum. K. Amen.</l><l xml:id="m-4458b641-091e-4d83-962b-67ed5303b067" facs="#m-de4ccdde-1556-4811-991c-eb57f0130116" label="text-like">The neophyte heeps this lightea</l><l xml:id="m-a4168f90-a16a-4786-aa03-bb7d2beacbf2" facs="#m-c1de343b-0ef4-4ccf-82a6-846bd9bd4e8c" label="lyrics-like">candle in his hand for the rest õf the</l><l xml:id="m-2e792b63-15e0-4e55-93cf-d19eef2a79cf" facs="#m-7de19963-ef7c-43e6-805f-aea8e32b0aae" label="ambiguous">ceremony except ivhen he receives</l><l xml:id="m-5f6dd025-9827-4301-ab41-c236a2dd8bc4" facs="#m-426f9d0f-1ada-46da-9b8d-2dc14828ca17" label="ambiguous">Confirmation.</l><l xml:id="m-47881807-8f19-42a9-9e48-b749a50e668e" facs="#m-a1d954d8-1835-4162-814e-21d334249011" label="text-like">The celebrant then says (in the plural if they are more than one):</l><l xml:id="m-dddbca54-0b8f-43c1-85c9-a14bb568fb53" facs="#m-db8448b4-4172-4bf2-a781-03a63e70bc22" label="lyrics-like">N. Vade (Ite) in pace, et Dóminus sit tecum (vobiscum).</l><l xml:id="m-ecd48c2e-3aff-4ea4-bd2e-0d939e993a86" facs="#m-b0fdf2fb-f946-4c9f-815f-dc6460838400" label="ambiguous">K. Amen.</l><l xml:id="m-43506942-fca8-4978-a6ab-29aa0074a5ed" facs="#m-6cb8e460-ae47-4056-bfc1-11bbf39f5e4a" label="text-like">If a bishop is present who can laufully confer the sacrament of Confir¬</l><l xml:id="m-c84390ae-e665-4052-8a5a-e7f59a97b255" facs="#m-d5f97965-59c8-48dc-b2fb-2fb11a7e0e52" label="text-like">mation, the neophytes receive it from him.</l><l xml:id="m-08947295-56e4-4bc2-8715-70ff5805a3e1" facs="#m-da271899-7cf0-499a-8297-71fdc50e556e" label="text-like">The neophytes devoutly receive Holy Communion at the Mass which</l><l xml:id="m-c02deb3b-627d-4c4c-8769-dc61d7dbc26a" facs="#m-f35fa75c-af92-4da1-8f83-6ea4cbb8dabd" label="ambiguous">follows.</l><l xml:id="m-e66f270e-6ed3-47b4-9cd7-e8d13d7bae75" facs="#m-ab62b2b8-6b5d-4381-b39f-9331b5ec501a" label="text-like">22. When the Blessing (and Baptism) is finished, the baptismal water</l><l xml:id="m-81446263-4ad5-4d0d-a421-2a7dc4f7bf01" facs="#m-8a5836ff-7ed3-42ae-ab7b-00edb1493ac3" label="text-like">is carried to the font, in procession. The celebrant puts incense in the thurible</l><l xml:id="m-2eb65d89-03fd-4b0a-8c5a-8de964c328bb" facs="#m-4c29677e-376c-4506-9cfd-9ccbf99f7d2f" label="text-like">and blesses ir. The procession tahes place as follouis:</l><l xml:id="m-bc998ad3-ac24-4f12-ad5d-a682d54de974" facs="#m-c46decac-949a-47a8-8f9a-b21e576e27ad" label="text-like">a) the thurifer goes first,</l><l xml:id="m-48a306c5-22ad-4f47-86ae-8ab1d2c94d0b" facs="#m-76f8d37d-5381-4b2a-8ab4-86c764e16b19" label="ambiguous">a) mne thurifer goes first,</l><l xml:id="m-1c652c1b-81a8-4b45-ac88-0a9a0522256b" facs="#m-c399a16a-8c0f-46fe-a5a0-983eb4cf8658" label="lyrics-like">bthen the subdeacõn or cleric mith</l><l xml:id="m-af014fa8-5b03-4de0-9015-0faa5a408021" facs="#m-5fde20cd-3d09-42e1-a0b2-66a5a350187e" label="text-like">b) then the cross-bearer,</l><l xml:id="m-514512d0-0c5c-4be8-9d91-86f6514466c9" facs="#m-d2f55e41-3388-4ada-bda6-fb1ab7fbfbd7" label="text-like">the cross,</l><l xml:id="m-972cfc0a-13be-4c45-b090-3b30813e6da5" facs="#m-3d2615cd-0e0d-4eb2-b7ca-a2606c3ff53f" label="text-like">c) then the servers,</l><l xml:id="m-2f6c8ad6-6e49-4371-899d-a62df6937a79" facs="#m-4d0cff20-c044-40f8-85f2-f379621c6469" label="text-like">e) the clergy,</l><l xml:id="m-e1b345c9-5410-4c9b-90e7-bb9247416588" facs="#m-4894aa80-69b3-4c06-a6f2-63041e4834bc" label="text-like">d) ihen tne deacon with the vessel</l><l xml:id="m-35753c48-1d84-4e9b-aa19-cb792b378817" facs="#m-bc5c6869-40c9-41a0-afb7-b60f04512697" label="text-like">) then one or more servers carrying</l><l xml:id="m-cc375ae9-ff2b-43ff-959d-d22083bc92e1" facs="#m-a54bb501-e6cb-4fa9-8ccc-93a104045ca8" label="text-like">the baptismal water,</l><l xml:id="m-cb161e59-1531-404c-8524-ec3744315d9f" facs="#m-475fc9cd-a537-4cfe-a948-7333690d358f" label="text-like">of woater — unless an acolyte</l><l xml:id="m-a391c164-17a8-4502-8e73-a40826068b39" facs="#m-66e44286-d93b-411f-a396-ce1595c5206d" label="ambiguous">carries it,</l><l xml:id="m-cb9d3f22-e17c-40be-9aac-549e598b448b" facs="#m-95d354d0-f9fa-443b-9023-15762f8ea1fa" label="text-like">e) finally the celebrant, uith hcad</l><l xml:id="m-c8b0f9b6-2704-45d5-a53c-71a60fee5370" facs="#m-5d727b51-4986-454c-bf7e-c2f77fc6b05d" label="text-like">e) finally the celebrant mith head</l><l xml:id="m-02c6c6a8-498f-4cf9-91be-036fe7692775" facs="#m-77612656-6bd3-4e51-8b3e-3594ccdfaf66" label="ambiguous">covered.</l><l xml:id="m-5143ccdd-838d-41c1-8467-49a0dc1946ea" facs="#m-61677a57-9585-4624-9799-d66c68119160" label="ambiguous">coveredl.</l><l xml:id="m-e24bf757-a0ea-4a2a-8a5f-7521a56a2c93" facs="#m-b86869d6-b6ff-4241-86c1-304d6ee80c72" label="text-like">The paschat candle remains in its place: meanhile the follouing is sung:</l><l xml:id="m-f0a933c8-6c42-40e0-8f84-18332c5a8654" facs="#m-2c73eebc-7231-4d2a-ae98-9d57904777ec" label="ambiguous">Ps. 41, 2-4</l><l xml:id="m-742237b5-83ac-4589-8b95-40b853fad45a" facs="#m-033d9e80-14fe-4cd3-926d-ee375525e044" label="ambiguous">Canticle</l><l xml:id="m-4040cdfd-6f0d-43ac-9831-840ca77ce32c" facs="#m-f0ba3c9a-04e2-4198-bb53-b7ceeef3717c" label="lyrics-like">"de-sí-de-rat</l><l xml:id="m-5d73b981-096a-42eb-a7a4-c96f5c67acc0" facs="#m-db3c1fd3-139d-4248-81a2-dfbe890d1bae" label="lyrics-like">ad fóntes</l><l xml:id="m-2130d2a3-6288-4962-9ced-1854350ad345" facs="#m-1be8c159-0dd7-4525-9f4c-14e2445e0fc4" label="lyrics-like">DIcut cér- vus</l><l xml:id="m-a3224e68-7e48-4bf1-98ab-dffb5c9660c6" facs="#m-b26dd594-b3f2-49f4-b3d5-a0352a93c87e" label="lyrics-like">i-ta de- síde-rat ánima mé-a</l><l xml:id="m-dc96c373-6efa-4a77-a1a1-d6bc4ee20a29" facs="#m-cf2e3e39-43ae-4bf7-9e61-270408f26589" label="lyrics-like">aquá- rum:</l><l xml:id="m-e0eea024-1c78-4a26-b994-a35cfb8d4258" facs="#m-98ef99ed-24cd-4588-886e-3d71903ea3c2" label="lyrics-like">V. Si-ti-vit ánima mé¬</l><l xml:id="m-e1453cf4-ee5d-45bb-9456-57a830d173ea" facs="#m-3ea16fc7-a32a-4545-ad55-863f1cd33fdb" label="lyrics-like">ad te, Dé¬ us.</l><l xml:id="m-4b010898-8dc6-40a5-8809-ce11aa5c6115" facs="#m-e3ba2255-5da3-431a-8f79-a9b862ce61b9" label="lyrics-like">ad Dé-um ví¬</l><l xml:id="m-accbd3c4-cd9f-42d5-bc65-cecc821d5b5d" facs="#m-a5453600-c3f8-49b3-b17c-f83040809e98" label="lyrics-like">quando vé-ni¬ am</l><l xml:id="m-6f6ce7c8-bba3-4b15-90e6-d9637981d04d" facs="#m-7dabb65a-b426-446d-9f30-f8f04a809fb6" label="ambiguous">a</l><l xml:id="m-631e96d1-4632-4e8a-975b-878f97f624d2" facs="#m-fbd12a8a-3a88-4f6d-968d-a78a165a906e" label="ambiguous">vum:</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>